          "then": {
            "not": {
              "required": [
                "result"
              ]
            },
            "required": [
              "error"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "A response to exactly one [`Request`].\n\nThe schema carries the `ok`/`result`/`error` invariant as an `if`/`then`\nrather than leaving it to convention. `required` in JSON Schema is\nunconditional, so the coupling between `ok` and its companions is only\nexpressible conditionally -- and without it the schema accepts\n`{\"ok\":true}` with no result, `{\"ok\":false}` carrying a result, and a frame\nwith both. A frontend generated from that schema would treat all three as\npossible and would fail on a null deref rather than on a rejected frame.",
