  "$id": "https://goonzu.rs/schemas/ops-api.json",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "Frame on the wire: a 4-byte big-endian length followed by that many bytes of UTF-8 JSON. Frames are NOT newline-delimited: log lines and player names are untrusted text that can contain newlines, and splitting on one would desynchronise the stream. A frame is a Response if and only if it has an `ok` member; anything else is an EventFrame routed by `subscription`. `ops.hello` must be the first request. An absent optional member is OMITTED, never sent as null. Integer members carry the non-standard `format` values `uint32` and `uint64`, which record the Rust source width. They are annotations, not registered JSON Schema formats, so a strict validator will warn about them; register them as no-ops before compiling. The width matters to a consumer because a u64 above 2^53 does not survive a round trip through a JavaScript Number.",
  "title": "GoonZu local ops API",
  "x-contract-version": 1
